{"review":{"at":"2026-11-03T13:04:59-06:00","size":"full","verdict":"fix","findings":[{"n":1,"kind":"fix","text":"The task folder has no `requirements.md`: the owner's asks behind this diff (phantom \"Thank you.\" reaching the chat, the stray \"undefined\" reply, the Whisper flags) exist only as truncated spawn titles in `session.jsonl` and in the minions' own folders under `session-f5eadae9/`. A fresh agent can't tell from this folder what was asked or whether it was met. Write the brief, with the owner's words linked, and list the three minion tasks (`minion-minion-phantom-gate`, `minion-minion-undefined-guard`, and the whisper flags) and their commits."},{"n":2,"kind":"fix","text":"`Servex/Servex.js:507-509` says the new `-mc 0 --suppress-nst` flags take effect after \"a Servex restart\", but whisper is detached and a restart *adopts* the running process with its old args (`Servex/Process.js:352`, `adopt()`). So the flags never apply until whisper-server itself is stopped and started again. Fix the comment and the minion's landing note to say \"stop and start whisper\" (`stop_server`/`start_server whisper`), and do that once so the change is actually live."},{"n":3,"kind":"note","text":"`ux/Dictate/chat.js:97-104`: `last_final_info` is never cleared after `deliver()` reads it. So a later spoken sentence that has no Whisper final of its own (the browser engine, or `ComposerMic`'s path if it doesn't fire `panel.dictate.on_whisper`) is judged on an old clip's duration and word probability. The blast radius is small (blocklist phrases only, as `doc/phantom-gate.md` says), but resetting it to `null` after each use is one line."},{"n":4,"kind":"note","text":"`ux/Dictate/chat.js:99-103` wraps `panel.dictate.on_whisper` by reassigning it. If anything assigns `on_whisper` again later (VoiceStrip wires its own at `VoiceStrip.js:38`), the gate silently loses its info and falls back to the echo-active branch only. A listener/event would be sturdier, but this works today."},{"n":5,"kind":"note","text":"A real, deliberate spoken \"Thank you.\" said while Recite is reading, or within 1.5 s after it stops (`echo_active()`), is dropped by design (`phantom-gate.js:190`). Nothing on screen says so: the drop happens before `DictateHealth.set` and is only a line in `ai/whisper/bucket.jsonl`. That's acceptable, but `doc/phantom-gate.md` should name this trade-off under \"Known gap\"."},{"n":6,"kind":"note","text":"`ux/Dictate/test/phantom-gate.mjs:235` keeps its own copy of the phrase list rather than the real `BargeIn.PHANTOM_PHRASES`. The reason is stated (BargeIn.js is browser-only), but the test can't catch a mismatch with the real `noise()`. For example, the real one doesn't trim, so a `\" Thank you.\"` with a leading space slips through both gates."},{"n":7,"kind":"note","text":"The `is_filler` doc comment at `Servex/agents/Sessions.js:1724` still lists only `(listening)`, punctuation and filler lines, not the new `undefined`/`null` case at line 1726."}],"branch":"worktree/qf-9","head":"209c73eee1c2d81dc6bacc14fb1160fedf9b7332","model":"claude-opus-5-5","cost":1.0276052,"file":"review.md","report":null,"shots":null}}
